From 12785beda78da31cde29086437b253d7a9a0c0de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gryphon397 <jgfillman@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 13:07:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] stoat: make the package typecheck so tsup can emit
 declarations
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three strict-mode failures blocked `tsup`'s DTS step, which is why our
Dockerfile builds this package with --no-dts. Without dist/index.d.ts the
consuming client can't resolve the module at all: 12x TS2307 plus ~13
cascading 'unknown' errors in packages/client.

- useConnectionStatus / useIsEncrypted: our own e283171 changed
  useEnsureRoom to return Room | undefined instead of throwing, but these
  two call sites were never updated. They passed a possibly-undefined room
  straight into the observer and dereferenced r().state. Both now fall back
  the way useObservableState already expects (it takes Observable | undefined
  and guards), so no-room renders stay disconnected/unencrypted rather than
  throwing.

- useIsSpeaking: ParticipantEvent.AudioLevelChanged does not exist in
  livekit-client 2.x (we're on 2.15.13). `p.on(undefined, handler)`
  registered a listener that could never fire, and the surviving
  IsSpeakingChanged handler only acted on the falling edge — so remote
  participants never lit up as speaking at all, in ParticipantTile and
  VoiceChannelPreview. IsSpeakingChanged now drives both edges, keeping the
  250ms hold that avoids mid-sentence flicker. The local-mic RMS path is
  unchanged. REMOTE_THRESHOLD is dropped as it is now unreachable.

- useIsSpeaking: buf[i] is number | undefined under noUncheckedIndexedAccess.

`tsup` now completes the DTS step and emits a 68 KB dist/index.d.ts.
